figure('gmr.png','Figure 3.2 Graphical model representation of attribution')
p('The GMR is a conceptual directed acyclic graph, not a fitted Bayesian network. Operator type A, task C and environment E influence behavior B. Behavior and measurement conditions generate observations O; features X then support prediction. Sensor quality Q affects what is observable. Environment includes tool/access conditions and can influence both behavior and observation. This makes explicit the route by which a classifier could recognize the environment rather than transferable operator behavior.')
p('Matching C and E reduces systematic arm differences. Canary tests assess Q. Actor/configuration holdouts test recurrence of informative patterns. Timing/tool ablations examine reliance on selected pathways. The graph explains the design but does not identify a causal effect of autonomy from predictive scores. There are no fitted edge weights or causal probabilities to report.')
tab('Table 3.2 GMR alignment with objectives',['Path or risk','Design response','Output'],[['A to B to O to X','Matched objectives and shared sensors','RQ1 feature ablations'],['E to B and O','Common access/tools; source probes','Shortcut audit'],['Q to O','Clock, canary and loss checks','Completeness and loss sensitivity'],['New actor/configuration','Group and family holdouts','RQ2 transfer and stability'],['X to class prediction','Same features and tuning limits','RQ3 scores, errors and cost']],[1.4,2.5,2.1])
h('3.4 Five Day Collection Protocol')
p('The pilot must validate resets, routes, sensors, evidence storage and autonomy labeling before formal collection. Each trial begins with a recorded snapshot ID, objective assignment and synchronization check. An independent recorder assigns actor truth from the execution manifest rather than classifier features. Objective success uses target state or an independent evidence criterion. Failed objectives remain eligible for attribution when the telemetry is valid.')
red('Illustrative daily allocation: 12 human and 12 AI primary trials, with 24 controls distributed across the period. Both arms and multiple tasks appear each day. Time caps, staffing, parallel ranges and exact collection dates remain unresolved. No one day is reserved for one label.')
tab('Table 3.3 Five day collection schedule',['Day','Planned emphasis','Acceptance record'],[['1','Balanced task set and reset checks','Manifests, canaries and clock/route audit'],['2','Counterbalanced repetition','Loss, intervention and exclusion audit'],['3','Equivalent task variants','Coverage and learning/carryover review'],['4','Balanced tasks including reserved groups','Sealed test-evidence check'],['5','Complete planned cells and controls','Raw hashes and deviation log']],[.45,2.7,2.85],redrows=True)
p('Reserved groups participate across the same days when feasible. A day-held-out stress analysis is separate from an unseen-operator test. Human task learning may change behavior across repeats; counterbalancing and participant grouping reduce but do not eliminate carryover. Objectives specify authorized discovery, controlled movement between designated systems and retrieval of a planted decoy artifact. The paper does not require releasing credentials or exploit instructions.')
h('3.5 Ground Truth and Validation')
p('Record trial ID, pseudonymous actor/configuration, checkpoint family, task variant, range snapshot, day, UTC start/end, intervention status and hashes. Keep scenario success separate from actor truth. Preserve raw logs, then produce normalized events and a versioned trial table. Validate time offsets and deduplicate by reliable source identifiers or documented composite keys; repeated commands are not automatically duplicate events. Missing arguments, truncation and absent sensors retain quality flags.')
red('Proposed pilot quality targets: at least 95% canary coverage, no unresolved label ambiguity, and timestamp error no greater than one second for features requiring that resolution. These are unmeasured discussion targets, not guaranteed sensor capabilities. Final gates depend on the chosen instrumentation.')
h('3.6 Exploratory Data Analysis')
p('Begin with label-blind integrity checks. Label-aware feature decisions use development data only; a custodian preserves the locked outcomes. Post-evaluation test plots are descriptive and cannot trigger unreported retuning. The provenance funnel reports scheduled, attempted, logged, valid and excluded trials by arm, group, task and day. Distinguish empty behavior from absent observation and report the number of independent groups.')
p('Summarize duration, event volume, missingness, duplicates, clock error and task success. For numeric features report nonmissing count, median, quartiles, extrema and robust spread. Plot shared-axis histograms or empirical cumulative distributions and stratify by group/task. Do not treat every event as an independent sample. Investigate outliers using provenance rather than removing them because they weaken a hypothesis.')
p('Assess dependence through Spearman correlations and group summaries. Explore relevance using training-fold distributions, univariate discrimination, grouped permutation and retrained ablation. High marginal separation may reflect source; weak marginal separation can coexist with useful interactions. Record inclusion/exclusion reasoning and retain the locked feature definition before final scoring.')
tab('Table 3.4 EDA outputs',['Output','Required view','Decision'],[['Provenance funnel','Counts by arm, group, day and reason','Design versus observed sample'],['Missingness','Feature by arm/group/day matrix','Collection artifact risk'],['Distributions','Median/IQR and common-scale ECDF','Overlap, skew and tail behavior'],['Dependence','Spearman matrix and group spread','Redundancy and pseudoreplication'],['Relevance','Permutation and retrained ablations','Incremental predictive value'],['Outcome strata','Task, success and trace length','Outcome/length shortcuts'],['Learning curves','Validation score versus training groups','Value of more independent collection'],['Source probe','Metadata-only/source classifier','Residual source distinguishability']],[1.2,2.65,2.15])
h('3.7 Feature Engineering')
p('The trial is the primary observation. Normalize target-side command/process tokens using a frozen vocabulary, removing identities and assigned experimental cues. Command diversity is distinct tokens divided by observed tokens. Transition entropy summarizes adjacent token-pair frequencies. Both depend on sequence length; report length and repeat analysis on equal-length prefixes. Missing streams do not have zero diversity, and fewer than two tokens cannot define transition entropy.')
p('Process breadth requires validated parent–child events. Network entropy uses protocol observations, while outward traffic fractions require a verified boundary mapping; flow forward/backward fields are not automatically outbound/inbound. Repetition is only a retry proxy unless failed actions and subsequent attempts can be linked. Controller-only statistics cannot silently substitute for target-side features.')
tab('Table 3.5 Feature dictionary draft',['Family','Definition','Validity check'],[['Diversity H1','Distinct normalized tokens / token count','Same parser and length sensitivity'],['Entropy H1','Adjacent-pair Shannon entropy','Length eligibility and frozen vocabulary'],['Host','Process breadth, authentication and error patterns','Validate sensors and parent joins'],['Network','Protocol mix, connections, boundary direction','Remove identities; verify direction'],['Timing','Rates, durations, interval CV and concurrency','Ablate all timing proxies together'],['Tool','Names and derived executable categories','Ablate categories as well as names'],['Quality','Coverage, missingness and truncation','Diagnostic unless explicitly qualified']],[1.0,2.7,2.3])
p('Imputation, scaling, encoding, clipping and selection are fitted inside training folds. Median imputation requires eligible training observations; zero-variance features need an explicit rule. Trees receive the same information even when scaling is unnecessary. Changing the feature schema creates a new version and requires a full rerun. Feature validity is established before comparing models.')
h('3.8 Grouped Evaluation and Baselines')
red('Illustrative split: eight human and eight AI configuration groups contribute 80 development trials; four human and four AI groups contribute 40 locked trials. AI configurations span the two supplied checkpoints if feasible. Family holdout is an additional analysis; two families do not establish generalization to arbitrary AI systems.')
p('Use inner group-aware folds for tuning and outer grouped development folds for estimation. Keep each participant/configuration together and track repeated task templates. If available groups cannot support the intended folds, revise the plan before scoring. Locked predictions are produced once after the candidate definitions and rules are frozen. Baselines include no-skill dummy and logistic regression; timing-only and metadata-only models are diagnostics. Scripted and benign controls are not relabeled as humans.')
red('Proposed budget: at most 20 hyperparameter configurations per candidate, common outer splits, three inner grouped folds where supported, and recorded wall-clock caps. Model repeat seeds are 19, 29, 39, 49 and 59. These settings are unexecuted and require freeze with actual group counts.')
h('3.9 How the Classifiers Work')
p('Logistic regression maps a linear combination of scaled features through a sigmoid to estimate AI probability. Regularization limits coefficient size. Coefficients are conditional model associations, not causal effects. H2 concerns above-baseline transfer after shortcut controls; it does not require logistic regression to win RQ3.')
p('An SVM seeks a separating margin with penalties for violations. C trades margin width against errors, and an RBF kernel permits nonlinear boundaries using distances between scaled features. Gamma determines how local those comparisons are. Raw SVM decision scores are not calibrated probabilities; calibration must use training-only grouped data (Cortes & Vapnik, 1995).')
p('A decision tree recursively selects thresholds that improve node purity. A terminal leaf supplies a class distribution or decision. Depth and leaf-size limits constrain complexity. A random forest averages randomized trees to reduce dependence on one partition (Breiman, 2001). Split-gain importance alone cannot establish H1; held-out ablation is required.')
p('XGBoost adds trees to improve a regularized objective, controlled by learning rate, depth, subsampling and penalties; early stopping observes training-internal validation (Chen & Guestrin, 2016). A tabular transformer embeds numeric features as tokens and learns interactions through attention. It receives the same feature table rather than raw text. The final implementation must be qualified against FT-Transformer (Gorishniy et al., 2021).')
tab('Table 3.6 Tuning specification',['Model','Dimensions to freeze','Protection'],[['Logistic','Penalty and regularization strength','Scaling inside training'],['Tree','Depth and minimum leaf size','Same grouped folds'],['Forest','Trees, depth, feature fraction and leaf size','Pinned bootstrap/RNG'],['XGBoost','Depth, learning rate, rounds and penalties','Internal early stopping'],['SVM','C, kernel and gamma','Scaled input; grouped calibration'],['Transformer','Width, depth, dropout, learning rate, epochs','Qualified implementation and seeds']],[1.0,3.0,2.0])
h('3.10 Equations and Metrics')
p('Let y = 1 denote autonomous AI and y = 0 denote human. TP is correctly identified AI, FP is a human labeled AI, FN is missed AI and TN is correctly identified human. Compute primary scores from one locked prediction per trial. Report group-balanced sensitivity scores separately. Undefined denominators are disclosed with support counts; software zero-division conventions are not evidence of certainty.')
E=[['1','m_j = n_missing,j / n','Missing fraction for feature j'],['2','D = |unique(c_1,…,c_N)| / N','Command diversity; N > 0'],['3','H = −Σ_ab p_ab log₂(p_ab)','Transition entropy; adjacent-pair frequencies; N ≥ 2'],['4','IQR = Q_0.75 − Q_0.25; CV = s / mean','Spread and variation; CV requires a meaningful positive mean'],['5','ρ_s = corr(rank(X),rank(Z))','Spearman correlation; average ranks for ties'],['6','z_j = (x_j−μ_train,j)/σ_train,j','Training-only scaling; zero variance handled explicitly'],['7','p(y=1|x) = 1/(1+exp[−(β₀+βᵀx)])','Logistic probability'],['8','L = −Σ_i w_i[y_i log p_i +(1−y_i)log(1−p_i)] + λ||β||²','Weighted logistic loss; intercept unpenalized'],['9','min ½||w||²+CΣ_i v_iξ_i; t_i(wᵀφ(x_i)+b) ≥ 1−ξ_i; ξ_i ≥ 0','Soft-margin SVM; t_i ∈ {−1,+1}; v_i sample weights'],['10','K(x,z) = exp(−γ||x−z||²)','RBF kernel; tune C and gamma internally'],['11','G = 1−Σ_k p_k²; ΔG = G_parent−Σ_child(n_child/n_parent)G_child','Gini impurity and split improvement'],['12','p_RF(x) = (1/B)Σ_b p_b(x)','Average B tree probabilities'],['13','L_XGB = Σ_i l(y_i,Σ_t f_t(x_i)) + Σ_t[γT_t+½λ||w_t||²]','Additive trees; leaf-count and leaf-weight penalties'],['14','Attention(Q,K,V) = softmax(QKᵀ/√d_k)V','Feature-token attention'],['15','Precision_AI = TP/(TP+FP); Recall_AI = TP/(TP+FN)','AI precision and sensitivity'],['16','Specificity_H = TN/(TN+FP); FPR_H = FP/(FP+TN)','Correct-human and false-AI rates'],['17','F1_AI = 2TP/(2TP+FP+FN); F1_H = 2TN/(2TN+FP+FN)','Class-specific F1'],['18','MacroF1 = (F1_AI+F1_H)/2; BA = (Recall_AI+Specificity_H)/2','Primary macro-F1 and balanced accuracy'],['19','Accuracy = (TP+TN)/(TP+TN+FP+FN)','Overall accuracy'],['20','ROC_AUC = Σ_k (FPR_k−FPR_(k−1))(TPR_k+TPR_(k−1))/2','Trapezoid integral over sorted ROC points'],['21','AP = Σ_k (Recall_k−Recall_(k−1))Precision_k','Average precision; step integration, not trapezoidal PR-AUC'],['22','Brier = (1/n)Σ_i(p_i−y_i)²','Probability loss; lower is better'],['23','w_i ∝ 1/(G_y n_g); normalize each class equally','Equal group contribution within class'],['24','Δ_j = F1_full−F1_without_j; PI_j = F1_original−mean_b F1_permuted_j,b','Retrained ablation versus permutation reliance'],['25','Transfer loss = F1_reference−F1_unseen','Descriptive gap; different populations can contribute'],['26','CI = [quantile_0.025(Δ*),quantile_0.975(Δ*)]','Paired group-bootstrap percentile interval'],['27','p_perm = (1+#{|Δ*_b| ≥ |Δ_obs|})/(B+1)','Two-sided paired permutation under justified exchangeability'],['28','p_(k) ≤ α/(m−k+1); stop at first nonrejection','Holm familywise correction for m contrasts'],['29','J(A,B) = |A∩B|/|A∪B|','Top-feature-set stability; declare k and tie handling'],['30','D_KS = sup_x |F_dev(x)−F_test(x)|','Descriptive distribution shift after test unlock'],['31','s = int(SHA256(master|component|fold|repeat)[0:8],16)','Deterministic 32-bit component seed; literal separators'],['32','Cost = Σ_service usage_service × rate_service','Measured usage and dated rates']]
tab('Table 3.7 Equation register',['Eq','Calculation','Meaning'],E,[.35,3.45,2.2])
p('ROC-AUC and average precision require continuous scores; calibration requires probabilities. Precision–recall values depend on prevalence. Report confusion counts, class supports and threshold with all scores. Resample independent groups, stratified by class, while preserving paired candidate predictions. Few held-out groups can produce unstable intervals; repeated seeds and event volume do not repair that shortage. Group-weighted scores are labeled separately from the primary trial-weighted analysis.')
h('3.11 Hypothesis Decision Framework')
p('H1 requires incremental contribution from the named features, not a high overall score. Freeze whether individual and joint benefits are required. H2 tests frozen logistic regression against a declared baseline on unseen groups with reduced features. H3 requires paired evidence that SVM exceeds each of four candidates. A lead in a rounded table is not sufficient. Failed models, ties and inconclusive contrasts remain reportable outcomes.')
red('Proposed discussion margins: 0.02 macro-F1 improvement for H1/H3; positive baseline benefit for H2; human false-AI rate no greater than 0.20 as an operational screen. These are provisional targets, not power-justified or institutional criteria. Freeze margins, baselines and adjustment families before final scoring.')
p('A permutation test requires exchangeability at the declared grouped unit; arbitrary label shuffling does not ensure validity. Record pairing, resampling units and whether intervals are descriptive or simultaneous. If the design cannot support reliable inference, limit the conclusion to exploratory estimates. No metric threshold is selected to make the assumed results pass.')
tab('Table 3.8 Required evidence for success',['Claim','Required evidence','Insufficient evidence'],[['H1','Frozen individual/joint ablations with supported benefit','Rank alone or post hoc winner'],['H2','Logistic baseline contrast on reserved groups; shortcut checks','Same-source score'],['H3','SVM paired advantage over every named comparator','Largest mean without uncertainty'],['Utility','Human FPR, AI recall and scripted/benign control behavior','Macro-F1 alone'],['Reproduction','Rerun from hashes, splits and environment','Seed alone'],['Novelty','Updated closest-work comparison','Unsupported first claim']],[.7,2.95,2.35])
h('3.12 Robustness and Seeding')
p('Robustness removes all timing-derived variables, removes tool names and derived categories, and combines both ablations. Additional analyses restrict command length, hold out tasks or days, and hold out checkpoint families where support exists. Sensor-loss perturbations evaluate random loss and contiguous outages. Shuffled group labels, metadata-only prediction and ordinary automation supply negative controls. Source-recognition models test residual collection differences.')
red('Proposed sensor-loss levels: 5%, 10% and 20%, using identical perturbations across candidate models. Proposed bootstrap/permutation counts: 2,000 and 1,000. Formal master seed: 20261024; model repeats: 19, 29, 39, 49, 59. These are unexecuted prospective settings. Illustration tables are hand-specified arithmetic examples, not seeded experimental predictions.')
p('Separate seeds for collection order, partitioning, tuning, fitting, bootstrap, permutation and synthetic generation. Derive component seeds using Equation 31 with UTF-8 encoding and explicit separators. Persist both seed inputs and integers; avoid language-default hash functions. Agent decoding seeds, if supported, are distinct from analysis seeds. Save explicit split manifests rather than trusting a seed to reproduce future library behavior.')
p('Set Python, NumPy and framework RNGs; log deterministic settings and unsupported operations. PyTorch warns that seeds do not guarantee identical results across releases or hardware (PyTorch contributors, n.d.). Preserve package versions, model/tokenizer digests, precision, GPU runtime/driver and thread counts. Computational reproduction reruns identical logs; experimental replication repeats the exercise and is not expected to produce byte-identical human or agent behavior.')
h('3.13 Governance and Execution Boundaries')
p('Human participation requires the appropriate institutional determination and consent process before collection; approval is not assumed. Restrict activity to authorized range resources and objectives. Credentials and identities remain in restricted evidence; publish sanitized aggregates under appropriate terms. The model artifacts, skills and external route must be auditable. No AWS range or autonomous attack was launched to create this manuscript.')
red('Approval identifiers, recruitment, retention period, publication permissions and cloud budget remain missing. Confirm the author’s November 14 review and December 1 defense targets with the program. GW currently expands AIR as Academic Integrity Review; reconcile the prior project label AI Review before submission.')
chap(4,'Results')
h('4.1 Evidence Status')
p('The completed synthetic engineering test and real-archive command screen are exploratory evidence. They are not the planned five-day matched target-side experiment. No formal H1/H2/H3 decision is available. This chapter retains those observed results separately from report-construction examples.')
p('ILLUSTRATIVE RESULTS: Red numbers are invented reporting examples or marked TO COMPUTE. They are not sampling-based estimates or experimental findings. No confidence interval, p-value or hypothesis pass is fabricated.',True)
h('4.2 Recorded Exploratory Evidence')
p('The real-archive screen used 111 GAMBiT windows from 57 participants, 1,315 Honey windows from nine model identifiers and 38 COCHISE windows from 15 model/configuration identifiers. Ten-command windows and five group-split seeds produced 1,464 real archived observations. These were controller-command records from different studies, not matched target-side trials. Saved aggregate verification and project tests passed (Pagan, 2026a).')
