h('4.6 Hypothesis Status')
p('H1, H2 and H3 remain pending formal collection and evaluation. The exploratory analyses motivate the experiment but do not confirm target-side claims. Report support, lack of support or inconclusive evidence according to the frozen framework, preserving controls and failure analysis. No illustrative table substitutes for missing evidence.')
chap(5,'Discussion and Conclusions')
h('5.1 Interpretation Framework')
p('The central question is whether separation reflects behavior under matched conditions or artifacts of the exercise. Strong full-feature performance with weak reduced-feature performance suggests timing/tool reliance. Strong within-configuration performance with weak transfer limits the claim to familiar agents. Frequent AI labels on scripts indicate difficulty separating autonomy from automation. The earlier archive analysis shows why high accuracy alone is inadequate.')
p('Stronger evidence combines held-out discrimination, acceptable human error, stable contributions, independent sensor validation and documented robustness. The matched design reduces source differences but does not guarantee their elimination. A numerical ranking cannot settle these measurement questions.')
h('5.2 Conditional Discussion')
p('ILLUSTRATIVE DISCUSSION FOR REPLACEMENT: In the constructed example, SVM reached macro-F1 0.825, AI recall 0.800 and human false-AI rate 0.150. Such a result would indicate useful but imperfect discrimination in the sampled range. It would not establish superiority without paired uncertainty and corrected comparisons, nor transport to actual adversaries or unseen environments.',True)
p('CONDITIONAL H1 TEXT: If frozen ablations show supported individual and joint improvements, diversity and entropy can be described as useful predictors in this setting. If only their joint contribution is supported, the conclusion must refer to the combination. If neither helps, report H1 as unsupported instead of substituting a favorable post hoc feature.',True)
p('CONDITIONAL H2 TEXT: Above-baseline reduced logistic performance on reserved groups would support a bounded transfer claim. Failure on the new checkpoint or removal of timing/tools would instead limit the result. Several prompts from one model do not establish generalization across model families.',True)
p('CONDITIONAL H3 TEXT: Support requires SVM to exceed every named comparator under the frozen corrected tests. A practical tie may justify choosing a cheaper model but does not support superiority. An unsupported H3 does not invalidate a supported feature finding or transfer result.',True)
h('5.3 Conclusions')
p('The work currently establishes a research design and auditable reporting structure, not completed evidence that target-side features reliably identify autonomous-AI APT-like activity. Existing exploratory evidence justifies a small matched pilot while demonstrating source-confounding risks. The final conclusion must state what the implemented experiment supports, including a negative or inconclusive outcome.')
p('CONDITIONAL FINAL CONCLUSION: Replace this paragraph with actual sample/group counts, the locked primary score and uncertainty, human false-AI rate, AI recall, transfer limits and the disposition of every hypothesis. If the evidence supports the thesis, constrain the claim to the observed laboratory and tested configurations. Otherwise describe the unsupported distinction or measurement limitation. All empirical conclusions here remain pending.',True)
h('5.4 Contributions to Knowledge')
p('The intended contribution is a protocol that connects a graphical dependency model to matched collection, defender-side feature extraction, grouped validation and explicit robustness tests. A second intended contribution is a qualified dataset or restricted evidence package with actor provenance and controls. A third is a scope-qualified model/feature comparison. These remain prospective until collection, qualification and appropriate release are completed.')
p('Prior work already addresses automation classes, AI-family fingerprints and shared-stimulus human–AI comparisons. The contribution is an extension in measurement and validation, not an asserted universal first. A well-supported negative result can clarify which apparent signatures fail when collection conditions are matched.')
h('5.5 Limitations and Future Work')
p('Future work should broaden independent participants, checkpoints, scaffolds and target networks and examine longitudinal drift. Vary hardware placement, prompts, skills and missing sensors systematically. Five-day laboratory scores should not be treated as deployment readiness. Operational evaluation requires external validation and realistic false-positive analysis.')
p('More rows may not be the best investment. If performance improves mainly with new groups, collect diverse operators rather than repeated windows. If instrumentation dominates, repair it first. If a task creates a shortcut, rematch the task instead of adding model complexity. These decisions should follow learning curves and quality audits rather than a preferred hypothesis outcome.')
h('5.6 Completion and Publication')
p('Replace red assumptions with verified protocol choices or remove them; populate results from locked predictions; recompute all uncertainty and adjusted comparisons; update the literature and verify full texts; and complete GW formatting, disclosure and approval checks. Preserve the author’s November 14 review and December 1 defense targets as planning dates until confirmed. The submission copy requires evidence-backed claims, not merely removal of red formatting.')
